<mujoco model="mid360">
  <!--
    Livox Mid-360 3D lidar: a standalone mount (primitive housing + a `mid360` scan site) for the
    `spawn_sensor` plugin, mounted on its own or by a robot manifest at the vendor joint origin.

    Every dimension is from the Livox Mid-360 User Manual v1.2 (2024), Appendix "Livox Mid-360
    Dimensions" (p. 19) and "Coordinates" (p. 12). The drawing dimensions 65.0 x 65.0 mm footprint,
    60.0 mm height, the point-cloud origin O 47.0 mm above the bottom face, the dome's base 39.5 mm
    above it, the connector axis 14.3 mm above it and 73.0 mm overall width with the connector. The
    dome and ring diameters and the connector diameter are not dimensioned; they are scaled from the
    same drawing (60.0 mm height = 511 px at 400 dpi): dome 44.7 mm wide at its 39.5 mm base and 60.0 mm
    tall, a sphere of radius 22.4 mm centred 37.6 mm above the bottom; the knurled ring 51 mm across
    from 32.7 to 39.5 mm; the M12 connector 13 mm across.

    Body-local axes are the manual's point-cloud axes O-XYZ (p. 12): the origin is O, z points out of
    the dome, and the connector points along -x. The mount body's origin is O, so the vendor joint
    origin a robot description gives for the sensor frame places this body directly, and the bottom
    (mounting) face is at z = -0.047.

    The housing is primitives only, so the device compiles in every checkout. Livox's STEP assembly
    converts into finer visual meshes (external/external_assets.yaml, `livox_mid360_meshes`; see
    MID360_MESH_LICENSE), which are git-ignored and are not referenced here.

    Scan parameters and the `frames:` entry for this site are in mid360.manifest.yaml.
  -->
  <compiler angle="radian" autolimits="true"/>

  <asset>
    <material name="mid360_body" rgba="0.82 0.82 0.84 1" specular="0.4" shininess="0.3"/>
    <material name="mid360_window" rgba="0.06 0.05 0.28 1" specular="0.7" shininess="0.7"/>
    <material name="mid360_connector" rgba="0.15 0.15 0.15 1"/>
  </asset>

  <worldbody>
    <body name="mount">
      <!-- 265 g (manual, "Specifications", p. 20). The manual gives no inertia: a uniform solid over
           the 65 x 65 x 60 mm envelope, centred at half height. -->
      <inertial pos="0 0 -0.017" mass="0.265" diaginertia="0.0001728 0.0001728 0.0001866"/>
      <!-- Finned body below the ring, bottom face at z -0.047. -->
      <geom name="mid360_body" type="box" pos="0 0 -0.03065" size="0.0325 0.0325 0.01635"
            material="mid360_body"/>
      <!-- Knurled ring the dome sits in, z -0.0143 .. -0.0075. -->
      <geom name="mid360_ring" type="cylinder" pos="0 0 -0.0109" size="0.0255 0.0034"
            material="mid360_body"/>
      <!-- Optical window: top at z +0.013 (60.0 - 47.0 mm). -->
      <geom name="mid360_dome" type="sphere" pos="0 0 -0.0094" size="0.0224" material="mid360_window"/>
      <!-- M12 connector on -x, protruding 8.0 mm (73.0 - 65.0), axis 14.3 mm above the bottom. -->
      <geom name="mid360_connector" type="cylinder" pos="-0.0365 0 -0.0327"
            quat="0.7071068 0 0.7071068 0" size="0.0065 0.004" material="mid360_connector"/>
      <!-- The point-cloud origin O, where the rays start. Keep in step with the manifest's `frames:`. -->
      <site name="mid360" pos="0 0 0" size="0.005"/>
    </body>
  </worldbody>
</mujoco>
